   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The IDB Invest operation consists of two transactions: (i) a loan of up to US$24 million for a term of 11 years, intended to partially fund the construction and start-up of Induglob S.A.&#x2019;s new household appliance production plant (the &quot;Company&quot; or &quot;Induglob&quot;) located in the south of Ecuador, which will be guaranteed by all the assets of the project to be financed; and (ii) an uncommitted facility for up to US$10 million over a 12-month period, to be guaranteed by Induglob&apos;s portfolio with eligible clients, which constitutes a new source of funding for the Company&apos;s working capital needs (the Project&quot;). The Project is aligned with the Government of Ecuador&apos;s plan to reactivate the local economy by encouraging investments that allow for a change in the country&#x2019;s production matrix.</narrative>
